  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query is epothilone D, a desoxy analog of patupilone. The highest-similarity evidence molecule (patupilone, Morgan 0.73) shows direct preclinical BBB penetration with high brain exposure, and this result strongly transfers to the query. Therefore the query is predicted to have meaningful CNS access.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct brain/plasma or CSF measurement for the exact query molecule.",
    "The epoxide-to-alkene difference between patupilone and the query may modestly alter transporter or efflux liability.",
    "Human CNS pharmacokinetic data for the query are not directly available."
  ],
